1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:07,330
Welcome to ACI Advanced Characterization and Instrumentation.

2
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:12,700
Before introducing ACI in more detail,

3
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:18,380
this slide provides a quick overview of the ISCE² organizational structure.

4
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:22,350
Here, you can see where ACI sits within the Institute.

5
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:26,100
ACI is led by our Division Director,

6
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:27,180
Andrew Lim.

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:28,670
In the next few slides,

8
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:33,680
I will introduce our team and highlight the key analytical capabilities and

9
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,280
shared scientific resources that we offer.

10
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,530
ACI is organised into three technical domains,

11
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:46,610
chromatography and mass spectrometry, X-ray spectroscopy and microscopy,

12
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:50,080
and NMR, physical and thermal characterisation.

13
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:55,400
Together, our domain leads and staff manage a broad range of shared

14
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,550
scientific resources and provide analytical and characterisation support,

15
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:01,960
as well as technical training,

16
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,060
to our research community.

17
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:07,710
Beyond supporting our internal R&D activities,

18
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:11,640
we also extend our capabilities to industry partners,

19
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:15,200
providing services such as material characterisation,

20
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:19,400
failure diagnostics, method development, consultancy,

21
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:20,410
and collaboration.

22
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:27,160
Through these capabilities, we aim to provide practical analytical solutions to support

23
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:29,090
different research and industry needs.

24
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:34,150
The ACI division is led by our division director,

25
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:38,500
Andrew Lim, and Ong Li Li as the Division Deputy Director.

26
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,770
And it comprises three technical domains,

27
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:44,620
each led by our respective domain lead.

28
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:49,160
The Chromatography and Mass Spectrometry domain is led by Mr.

29
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:52,470
Ong Wai Chung, supported by our instrument specialists,

30
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,970
Ng Fu Song and Tan Kuan Yi.

31
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:59,080
The X-ray Spectroscopy and Microscopy domain is led by Ms.

32
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,450
Angeline Seo, together with three senior domain specialists,

33
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,080
Wang Zhan, Chia Sze Chen,

34
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,880
and Cao Xun, who specialize in XPS,

35
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,900
XRD and TEM respectively.

36
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:15,190
Ong Li Li also served as the domain lead of NMR,

37
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:21,340
Physical and Thermal Characterisation, supported by instrument specialists Yeo Wen Cong and

38
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,110
Kuan Kai Cong.

39
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:25,850
Beyond our analytical and characterisation work,

40
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:31,720
ACI also plays an important role in managing shared scientific resources across

41
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:32,520
the Institute.

42
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,880
Our responsibilities include equipment booking,

43
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,130
utilisation and charging, demand aggregation,

44
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:41,740
scientific equipment and systems refresh,

45
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,880
and equipment lifecycle management.

46
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,530
We also support digitalisation and sustainability initiatives.

47
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:54,990
Together, these activities help ensure that our scientific resources are effectively managed,

48
00:02:55,490 --> 00:03:00,360
optimised, and kept relevant to support the evolving research needs across the

49
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,160
Institute.

50
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:08,080
This slide gives you an overview of where our ACI laboratories are

51
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,480
located within the Institute.

52
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:15,430
Our eight analytical laboratories are conveniently located together on level 1.

53
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:20,100
Chromatography and Mass Spectrometry is based in Lab 1-01.

54
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:24,800
X-ray spectroscopy and microscopy is located in Labs 1-02,

55
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:31,200
1-03 and 1-06, while NMR Physical and Thermal Characterisation is based in

56
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,890
Labs 1-04 and 1-05.

57
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:38,200
Labs 1-07 and 1-08 are shared laboratories with other R&D divisions.

58
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:44,560
Having our analytical capabilities located close to one another makes it easier

59
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:49,680
for our teams to provide integrated analytical support for a wide range

60
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:50,720
of research needs.

61
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,400
Let's now take a closer look at our three technical domains,

62
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:59,270
starting with chromatography and mass spectrometry.

63
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:02,150
This domain brings together three key areas,

64
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:06,460
gas chromatography, liquid chromatography, and mass spectrometry.

65
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:10,200
These complementary techniques allow us to separate,

66
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:14,030
identify, and analyze a wide range of chemical compounds,

67
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:18,970
supporting both routine testing and more complex analytical investigations.

68
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:23,640
In the following slides, I will briefly introduce some of the key

69
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:28,050
analytical capabilities and instrumentation available within this domain.

70
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:34,040
Within this domain, we have a broad range of instruments to support

71
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:35,390
different analytical needs.

72
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:42,790
For gas chromatography, our capabilities include conventional GC with TCD and FID

73
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:47,370
detectors, comprehensive two-dimensional GC, or GC×GC,

74
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,060
as well as GC-MS equipped with pyrolysis,

75
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,270
which can be used for microplastic analysis,

76
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:57,250
thermal desorption, and headspace capabilities.

77
00:04:58,110 --> 00:05:02,440
We also have a refinery gas analyzer with a grab sampling system

78
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,780
for gas analysis.

79
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:09,930
For liquid chromatography, we have HPLC systems equipped with different detectors.

80
00:05:10,730 --> 00:05:16,170
We also have GPC systems using either THF or aqueous system,

81
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:18,730
depending on the solubility of the samples.

82
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:24,900
Our combustion ion chromatography capability supports the quantification of halogens,

83
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:27,290
anions and cations in solid,

84
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,100
liquid, and gas samples.

85
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,860
For more advanced mass spectrometry,

86
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,610
we have LC-QTOF-MS

87
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:36,270
and high-resolution LC-MS/MS

88
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,480
using the Q Exactive Orbitrap,

89
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:42,880
supporting both targeted and non-targeted analysis.

90
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:49,040
Finally, for elemental analysis, we have ICP-MS and ICP-OES,

91
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:53,350
supported by microwave digestion for sample preparation.

92
00:05:56,250 --> 00:05:58,790
Moving on to our second technical domain,

93
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:02,380
X-ray Spectroscopy and Microscopy, led by Ms.

94
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:03,180
Angeline Seo.

95
00:06:03,890 --> 00:06:07,500
Here, you can see some of the key instruments available within this

96
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:08,300
domain.

97
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:11,300
We have SEM and TEM,

98
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:15,730
which allow us to examine the morphology and structure of materials at

99
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:17,270
very small length scales.

100
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:23,150
We also have SAXS and WAXS for studying material structures and XPS

101
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:26,040
for surface elemental and chemical analysis.

102
00:06:26,810 --> 00:06:32,140
In addition, our Powder X-ray diffractometer is equipped with a reaction chamber

103
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:34,310
for in situ XRD studies,

104
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:38,780
allowing us to monitor structural changes under reaction conditions.

105
00:06:39,610 --> 00:06:45,530
We also have XRF with mapping capability for elemental analysis and distribution.

106
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:50,780
Together, these instruments provide complementary information on the morphology,

107
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:56,060
structure, surface chemistry, and elemental composition of different materials.

108
00:06:58,140 --> 00:06:59,980
Looking more closely to this domain,

109
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:03,330
we can broadly group our instruments into three areas.

110
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:09,720
For X-ray characterisation, we have powder X-ray diffraction with an in-situ reaction

111
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,860
chamber, X-ray fluorescence with mapping capability,

112
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:16,790
as well as small and wide-angle X-ray scattering,

113
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:18,450
or SAXS and WAXS.

114
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:25,020
For electron microscopy, we have SEM with EDS and BEX capabilities.

115
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:29,620
and TEM with advanced capabilities including Cryo-TEM,

116
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,630
EDS, 3D tomography and EELS.

117
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:38,220
We also have 3D X-ray micro-CT and atomic force microscopy,

118
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:42,270
allowing us to examine materials across different length scales.

119
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:45,550
For surface and molecular characterisation,

120
00:07:45,930 --> 00:07:48,610
we have XPS and Raman spectroscopy,

121
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:51,750
both with in situ gas reaction capabilities.

122
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:57,310
Moving on to our third technical domain,

123
00:07:57,710 --> 00:08:00,640
NMR, physical and thermal characterisation.

124
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:04,460
Our capabilities can broadly be divided into two areas.

125
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:07,380
The first is Nuclear Magnetic Resonance,

126
00:08:07,810 --> 00:08:14,240
or NMR, where we have liquid-state NMR spectrometers for molecular structure identification,

127
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:17,970
structural characterisation, and quantitative analysis.

128
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:20,270
The second is our thermal,

129
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:23,010
chemical, and physical characterisation laboratory.

130
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:27,720
which houses a wide range of instruments for evaluating the thermal behavior,

131
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:31,880
physical properties, and other characteristics of different materials.

132
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:36,700
Together, these capabilities allow us to look at materials from both a

133
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:39,020
molecular and bulk property perspective,

134
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,520
providing complementary information to support research,

135
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:45,250
product development, and problem solving.

136
00:08:47,350 --> 00:08:49,310
Looking more closely at third domain,

137
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:52,940
our capabilities can be broadly grouped into three areas.

138
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:59,890
First, for NMR, we have liquid-state NMR spectrometers equipped with both iProbe

139
00:08:59,990 --> 00:09:05,630
and cryoprobe, supporting molecular structure characterisation and quantitative analysis.

140
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:09,630
The second area is chemical and physical characterisation,

141
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:14,200
where we have a wide range of instruments for measuring different material

142
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,000
properties.

143
00:09:15,590 --> 00:09:17,950
These include surface area and pore size,

144
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:22,820
particle size, rheology, spectroscopy, dispersion and stability,

145
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:26,710
as well as mechanical and thermal conductivity measurements.

146
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,490
The third area is thermal analysis,

147
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:32,720
where our capabilities include TPDRO,

148
00:09:33,090 --> 00:09:39,240
simultaneous DSC-TGA and DSC, allowing us to study how materials behave and

149
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,560
change under controlled temperature conditions.

150
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:47,720
Together, these complementary techniques allow us to characterize materials from their molecular

151
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,790
structure through to their physical,

152
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:54,520
chemical, and thermal properties, giving us a more comprehensive understanding of the

153
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,700
samples we analyze.

154
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:02,820
To summarize, this slide brings together the wide range of analytical capabilities

155
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:06,870
available within ACI across our three technical domains.

156
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,940
With this broad range of complementary techniques,

157
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:14,220
we are able to support different types of samples and analytical needs.

158
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:19,300
More importantly, our team can work with you to identify the most

159
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:22,890
appropriate analytical approach for your specific research needs.
